      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just by curiosity, I dug what's going on.\n* Loading and pasting of previously created noodles are possible.\n* Output port of `UnityEngineComponent.__GetComponent__T` is typed `UnityEngine.Object`. \"Instance\" port of `SendCustomNetworkEvent` is typed `VRC.Udon.Common.Interfaces.IUdonEventReceiver` So it isn't connectable. (because not assignable each other)\n* If output port is typed `System.Object`, they are connectable. So new Graph Editor's type system itself seems to be fine.\n* Old (current live) editor `UdonGraph.CanConnect(Slot fromSlot, Slot toSlot)` returns `true` if `(fromSlot.node.name.Contains(\"__T\") || fromSlot.node.name.Contains(\"__TArray\"))` . So it is connectable. (This should be at least endWith imo)\n* Series of GetComponent methods seems to be the only cases that have parameterized output type with generics among defined nodes.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
